The V* specification tree is dual-licensed. Paths below are relative
to THIS FILE, so they hold both in the source repository (where this
file is `spec/LICENSE`) and on the published mirror (where this
directory is the repository root).

  Spec text — the normative Markdown under a version directory
  (`v*/**/*.md`, excluding `v*/conformance/**` and `v*/CHANGELOG.md`):
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0). Full
  text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
  Each such file also carries an SPDX-License-Identifier header, so
  the scoping survives a file being copied out of the tree.

  Everything else in this tree: MIT License, text below. That is the
  conformance corpus (`v*/conformance/**` — the corpus glob wins over
  the spec-text glob, so the READMEs and `.notes.md` files inside it
  are MIT too), the behavior fixtures (`behavior/**`), the registry
  tables (`registry/**`), the release tooling (`.github/scripts/**`)
  and its output (`v*/CHANGELOG.md`), and this tree's own front
  matter and lint configuration (`README.md`,
  `.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc`). These are test data, generated
  artifacts, tooling and repository front matter, not normative text.
  None of them carries an SPDX-License-Identifier header: the fixtures
  are byte-exact test data, JSON has no comment syntax, and the
  scripts and Markdown follow the same rule — so a file in this tree
  with no header is MIT, not unscoped.

Anything outside this tree — the reference implementations and the
contributor documentation — is MIT; see the LICENSE at the root of
the source repository, https://github.com/hop-top/poly-vstar.

